{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Kilayim.</b> Wheat and barley and grape-kernel in a hand-sweeping (Berakhot 22)." "<b>Lest it be forbidden.</b> As its Targum renders: 'תִּסְתָּאַב.' Anything that is detested by a person, whether for praise such as consecrated property, or for disgrace such as a prohibition — the term קִדּוּשׁ applies to it, as in ״אַל תִּגַּשׁ בִּי כִּי קִדַּשְׁתִּיךָ״ (Isaiah 65)." "<b>The fullness.</b> This is its padding and the extra that the seed adds."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:59.306634798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}